in the middle of the night a sudden  massive explosion  and a fireball blindingly bright even on  this grainy footage  it happened just before 4am in the built  up Harbor area of Saint Helia an entire  block of flats raised to the ground we  have a three-story building that has  completely collapsed  described as from a demolition point of  view probably as a pancake that has just  dropped almost sort of straight down the  as you will have seen I'm sure from some  of the pictures that are already  circulating it is a considerable  destruction  but in terms of casualties the scale of  the destruction is not yet known as many  as a dozen are believed to be missing  and it's feared there may be more  fatalities  my thoughts and prayers are foremost  with the families of those who have died  and those who are still waiting for news  of their loved ones and those who also  have been forced from their homes today  I want to offer my sincerest and  heartfelt thanks to our emergency  service responders who have been on the  scene since the early hours of this  morning and all of those who have worked  to make the site safe enough to begin  the search process  specialist teams from the UK have  arrived to help that process which will  continue throughout the night but police  have warned it may take days given the  extent of the rubble a huge operation is  also underway to make the site safe with  pockets of fire still reportedly burning  while dozens of local residents have  been evacuated and taken to the town  hall because of the damage to  neighboring buildings some of those at  the Town Hall came here having had their  Windows blown in others just had to grab  whatever clothing they couldn't put it  on and uh  with their pets some people came didn't  even grab their phones they just came  straight down here what caused this  blast is still not known but the fire  service confirmed it was called to the  area on Friday evening around eight  hours earlier after residents reported  smelling gas police say that will now be  the focus of their investigation
 

